'' strptr and sadd of a 'string * N' -- and a 'string * N' handed to a 'zstring ptr'
'' parameter -- are the STORAGE ADDRESS. They were fb_StrAllocTempDescF: a slot of the
'' runtime's 256-slot temporary-descriptor pool per call, never given back. tracks'
'' recv loop drained it within seconds of live TWS data. Measured, fbc-modern prints
'' ' 0 0 0 0', ' 0' and 'null buffers 0 pool alive 5' for this source; the old tiko
'' printed ' 2748 0' for the last line -- 2748 NULL buffers, and a dead pool that had
'' emptied its own labels.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/strptr-fixed-no-temp.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 TAKEZ(@fs)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call i32 TAKEZ(@temp_buffer)
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrAllocTempDescF(
